    <item>
      <title>Tokenization</title>
      <link>https://sameepkathayat.com.np/tokenization/</link>
      <pubDate>Thu, 23 Jul 2026 08:11:18 +0545</pubDate>
      <guid>https://sameepkathayat.com.np/tokenization/</guid>
      <description>&lt;p&gt;&#xA;We know, computers work with numbers and numbers only. So, whenever we represent some other formats like Emojis or Strings, it is naturally represented using numbers inside the computer system.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;&#xA;The same goes for LLMs. They can&amp;#39;t just work on raw text. They are first converted to numbers before they can be processed. The tool that does this exactly is known as a tokenizer. It is quite similar in concept but different than tokenizer used by compilers.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
